a parenthesised assignment target must not be loaded.

FOUR CHARACTERS, AND THE SECOND ONE SEGFAULTED:

    ln += 4;      correct, and always was
    (ln) += 4;    the variable was LOADED and the store wrote through its
                  VALUE as if that were an address

Every load decision in cc_core.c blanks the load when an assignment follows,
and each finds out by looking at the NEXT TOKEN. For `(ln) += 4` the next
token is the closing parenthesis, so not one of them saw it. This is the
seventh copy of that rule -- zzc, zzg, zzm, zzo, zzzh and zzzk are the others,
and every one was found separately, in CI.

WHAT IT COST. tcc reaches it through a macro, which is why the spelling is
parenthesised at all -- parentheses are how a macro parameter is written
safely:

    #define dwarf_read_4(ln,end) \
        ((ln) + 3 < (end) ? read32le(((ln)+=4) - 4) : 0)      tcc.h:1863

tcc_eh_frame_hdr walks .eh_frame with that macro, and it runs for EVERY
DYNAMIC OUTPUT:

    mc-tcc -nostdlib -static ...   fine
    mc-tcc -nostdlib ...           SIGSEGV
    mc-tcc -nostdlib -shared ...   SIGSEGV

That is the whole libc-facing surface stage 4 needs, and it is the crash
tcc-two-ways reports at "SUBJECT does it compile anything at all". The
hermetic job never sees it because that job is `-nostdlib -static` end to end.

HOW IT WAS FOUND. Bracketed inside mc-tcc with printf probes:
elf_output_file -> bind_libs_dynsyms (clean, all 177 symbols) ->
tcc_eh_frame_hdr -> crash on the FIRST loop iteration -> the macro. Then
reduced from the outside until the whole thing was three lines. The control
matters here: a gcc-built tcc given the identical command answers
`error: _start not defined` -- a clean diagnostic, no fault -- so the source
is fine and the fault is ours.

TWO GUARDS, AND BOTH ARE THE SAME RULE THE FILE ALREADY CARRIES.

  A DEREFERENCE OUTSIDE THE PARENTHESES CANCELS IT. In `*(t) = v`, `t` is NOT
  the target -- what it points at is -- so t must be loaded to be followed.
  The first attempt at this patch suppressed that load too and broke case 49,
  which has covered `*(t) = v` since before this flag existed.
  num_dereference_after_postfix is zero exactly when the parentheses are the
  whole target.

  NESTED PARENTHESES INHERIT IT. `((k)) += 2` enters the branch twice; the
  inner parenthesis sees only a `)` after itself and would clear what the
  outer one set. Saved and restored, the same shape Address_of uses four
  lines above.

WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM. `*(p)++` -- dwarf_read_1, on the same walk -- is a
DIFFERENT defect wearing the same parentheses: it needs the address for the
increment and the pre-increment value for the dereference, and suppressing the
load fixes the advance while breaking the value. Case 119 carries it as a
declared gap. tcc_eh_frame_hdr now reads a byte without advancing rather than
faulting, which is progress and is not a fix.

MEASURED, LOCALLY, EITHER SIDE:

    difftest amd64        98 -> 99 pass, 0 fail, 2 known gaps   (case 118 new)
    difftest aarch64     100 -> 101 pass, 0 fail, 2 known gaps
    stage 2 corpus       419 of 426                             unchanged
    tests2 through mc-tcc 90 of 105                             unchanged
    self-compilation      gen2.o == gen3.o == gen4.o            unchanged
    archive round trip    still links and runs                  unchanged

    mc-tcc -nostdlib          21821-byte dynamic executable
    mc-tcc -nostdlib -shared   2875-byte shared object

and the shared object is structurally identical to the gcc-built control's --
same dynamic section offset, the same thirteen entries, the same values.

